{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CdsXFwSiMEAYM5KdvTrDp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stage S1 for trial e6-t12 is complete. All four deliverables are written in the workspace root, and the ledger records the five node events (observe-package → infer-distinctions → estimate-value → self-check-spec → return-spec) with no `complete` event, as required.\n\nWhat the inference concluded:\n\n**Distinctions (4).** The task decomposes into four independent, purely computational questions over `server.log`: Q1 the 5xx count and Q2 the busiest hour (both mapped to E-A), Q3 the top IP under the lexicographic tie-break (E-B), and Q4 the longest inter-request gap in whole seconds (E-C). None of the task's evidence requirements impose authorship, access, or isolation conditions — admissibility only demands faithful derivation from the log. So every distinction is `locally_resolvable=true` and all other latent-structure features (`requires_isolation`, `contamination`, `capability_bearing_artifact`, `spans_sessions`) are false: reading the package destroys nothing here, and no capability-bearing artifact or cross-session state is needed.\n\n**Value estimates.** Since a single worker can satisfy all evidence requirements admissibly on its own, extra processes can only produce duplicate evidence. I estimated `local` at delta_e 1.0 / redundancy 0.0; `local-independent-verify` and `isolated-child` both at delta_e 0.75 / redundancy 0.5, because their second process re-derives what the worker already establishes; and `branching` at delta_e 0.95 / redundancy 0.05, expecting the run-time choice to collapse to the local branch. Governance risk is 0.0 across the board — everything runs under deterministic governance machinery and I have no concrete reason to expect a formal failure.\n\nThe self-check node re-read both JSON artifacts against their schemas and passed (recorded in the ledger as non-authoritative). Per protocol I did not solve the task itself; topology selection now falls to the deterministic ranker downstream."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1467,"cache_read_input_tokens":43029,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1467},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4701f397-e6a8-4e61-9ae0-e60364875ede","uuid":"70697558-8874-4bf4-b331-3b07fd682299","timestamp":"2026-08-09T16:53:10.851Z","request_id":"req_011CdsXFufKBacqzz4tfqsbh"}
